<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:14:12Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>DR Congo, Rwanda clash over Francophonie leadership as Macron seeks compromise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d7c33a8f960d6ff0279e80cc3294542f16a36516106eecdc6864448f15ca193</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:13:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T14:54:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261114-dr-congo-rwanda-clash-over-francophonie-leadership-as-macron-seeks-compromise--8dd812a22403.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261114-dr-congo-rwanda-clash-over-francophonie-leadership-as-macron-seeks-compromise" /><summary type="html">DR Congo and Rwanda clashed Saturday over the leadership of the Francophonie, as tensions between the neighbouring countries spilled into the race to head the 53-member organisation. French President Emmanuel Macron urged Rwanda to withdraw its candidate in favour of a compromise choice ahead of Monday's vote.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>'I never imagined my father was a Nazi': Born in a German-run 'baby factory'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3e3b8259c96791266cb572077f1db26280ab3cfdb6d46c1490c02f930a2275e</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:13:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T13:25:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261114-i-never-imagined-my-father-was-a-nazi-born-in-a-german-run-baby-factory--a90ba69f5562.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261114-i-never-imagined-my-father-was-a-nazi-born-in-a-german-run-baby-factory" /><summary type="html">Two trainloads of children, some of them born in Nazi-run "Lebensborn" maternity homes, were brought from Germany to Commercy in eastern France in 1946. One of them was Édith Pagot.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>USA: All passengers survive after tanker hits docked river cruise ship in New Orleans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:708ee2a38c5f93cd0b3c5737ffd908f9cd5bdf1ae4cfc7d1837b8cc4a3d41fba</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:13:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T13:15:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/usa-all-passengers-survive-after-tanker-hits-docked-river-cruise-ship-in-new-orleans--196361a3fb34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/usa-all-passengers-survive-after-tanker-hits-docked-river-cruise-ship-in-new-orleans" /><summary type="html">A portion of the Mississippi River remains closed after a collision between an oil tanker and a riverboat forced a chaotic river rescue in Louisiana. Story by Caitlin Brown.</summary></entry><entry><title>Inside Ethiopia's war: Rare access to a hospital treating victims of renewed fighting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4664c5f311d35bfca09329e74ee05d58a0ac341ab4d740d0a95754ddf0d3b374</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:13:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T12:23:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/inside-ethiopia-s-war-rare-access-to-a-hospital-treating-victims-of-renewed-fighting--64d2eb5d22c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/inside-ethiopia-s-war-rare-access-to-a-hospital-treating-victims-of-renewed-fighting" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia's renewed conflict is taking an increasing toll on civilians, with humanitarian organisations reporting a rise in casualties. In the Amhara region, FRANCE 24’s correspondent Tom Canetti was granted rare access to a civilian hospital where surgeons are struggling to treat the influx of wounded patients. But for many caught in the fighting, reaching medical care is a challenge in itself.
 
Warning: The report contains images of surgery that may be confronting for some viewers.</summary></entry><entry><title>Who are the 'street medics' showing up at protests around the world?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb036ad315c7ec5415d8eeed3b3a9d0a524f459dbef12e6b4ce1d44f7c6b0cf3</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:13:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T12:19:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/who-are-the-street-medics-showing-up-at-protests-around-the-world--0c414d784e65.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/who-are-the-street-medics-showing-up-at-protests-around-the-world" /><summary type="html">From treating tear gas exposure to tending to injuries, street medics have become an increasingly common sight at protests all over the world. But who exactly are they and when did they start showing up at demonstrations? Story by Daniel Quinlan.</summary></entry><entry><title>U2 releases first new studio album in a decade, 'Caranaval de Luz'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b251da2362731685930e2c67c5134daa4d34cec48ade47a998a13fd425f0220</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:13:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T12:17:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/u2-releases-first-new-studio-album-in-a-decade-caranaval-de-luz--7856f7336f02.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/u2-releases-first-new-studio-album-in-a-decade-caranaval-de-luz" /><summary type="html">U2 just released a new album after nine years of no new content. And fans are already rocking out to the new songs. Details on the Irish rock band’s comeback by Ophelie Jacobson.</summary></entry><entry><title>Half a million people gather for an open-air mass by Pope Leo in Peru</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae9809d805e9674460b677cfc7cd61c73983ee96fbb61268aafef2b429a98f96</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:13:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T11:17:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/half-a-million-people-gather-for-an-open-air-mass-by-pope-leo-in-peru--865ee0c1d4cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/half-a-million-people-gather-for-an-open-air-mass-by-pope-leo-in-peru" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo said it was a "joy to be back" in his second home of Chiclayo, where he made his name as a bishop. This is the latest stop on his South America tour, the very tour that saw fears of cancellation after the Pope underwent surgery for lung cancer. Story by Vedika Bahl.</summary></entry><entry><title>Microsoft's widespread outages caused global chaos, including in the healthcasre industry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49cbf80b1da9a5356eb930acf1137235261d2aa41f0bc815d3688e4ab54c4e01</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:13:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T11:07:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/microsoft-s-widespread-outages-caused-global-chaos-including-in-the-healthcasre-industry--b5a2d510401d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/microsoft-s-widespread-outages-caused-global-chaos-including-in-the-healthcasre-industry" /><summary type="html">Microsoft says it is seeing improvements in its service availability after an hours-long disruption knocked out its platforms including Outlook and Teams. The outage has affected hundreds of millions of people across the globe. The healthcare industry was among those impacted, as Ophelie Jacobson explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>France fend off South African comeback to clinch long-awaited win in Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d563168f459761cabdb70f4ae088b33814beaa19b04f43f89ca0b512ac5e2473</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:13:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:58:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261114-france-fend-off-south-african-comeback-to-clinch-long-awaited-win-in-paris--eb24a1ccaa69.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261114-france-fend-off-south-african-comeback-to-clinch-long-awaited-win-in-paris" /><summary type="html">Twenty-one years after last beating the Springboks in Paris, Les Bleus held out for a 21-19 win over the world champions on Friday after a nailbiting finale. Antoine Dupont and company are now one step away from reaching the Nations Championship final in London.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>US proposed Ukraine cedes Donbas in exchange for joining NATO, Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:459968ee36563ebc9b73ff9fa241601cfa71e63dc37b3d345270e80b07b767d2</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:13:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:30:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261114-us-negotiators-suggest-ukraine-cedes-territory-in-exchange-for-nato-membership--b3597e97289d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261114-us-negotiators-suggest-ukraine-cedes-territory-in-exchange-for-nato-membership" /><summary type="html">President Zelensky said the US had proposed ceding Ukraine's eastern city of Donbas to Russia, in exchange for Ukrainian membership of NATO, following the latest round of peace talks in Abu Dhabi this week. He reiterated that Kyiv was not willing to retreat from its territory and warned that the Kremlin's bid to change the continent's security architecture could lead to more wars.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Climate action is alive': Triumphant Democrats attend COP31 summit shunned by Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0bbcbb9c9c5a55d8f6155be9d8f4be32cb15b1a4d93db18fc32860f693cdb916</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:13:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:25:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/environment/20261114-climate-action-is-alive-triumphant-democrats-take-on-cop31-shunned-by-trump--38a7ef55fd3b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/environment/20261114-climate-action-is-alive-triumphant-democrats-take-on-cop31-shunned-by-trump" /><summary type="html">A delegation of 18 Democratic lawmakers arrived at the COP31 climate summit in Turkey on Saturday to reaffirm the US commitment to tackling global warming following their sweeping midterm election victory.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>SpaceX's Starship encounters problems during 15th test flight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:503bca1e39099657ef96dc04e2f839fab01bda055e72cea3702e603d712f1700</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:13:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:21:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spacex-s-starship-encounters-problems-during-15th-test-flight--0ef99121135e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spacex-s-starship-encounters-problems-during-15th-test-flight" /><summary type="html">Elon Musk’s SpaceX successfully launched its Starship, the world's largest spaceship, into orbit where it should release 15 satellites for its Starlink network. A few minutes after lift off however, the rocket's booster which was meant to return to the pad splashed down in the Gulf of Mexico. Details by Daniel Quinlan.</summary></entry><entry><title>Can Nvidia survive without tech titan Jensen Huang?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dde671524b506ecc596f309a39f9a79d6f67f15c5776ce286f52665cf283facb</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:13:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:20:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/can-nvidia-survive-without-tech-titan-jensen-huang--9cf2241e07bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/can-nvidia-survive-without-tech-titan-jensen-huang" /><summary type="html">The Financial Times says computing giant Nvidia has approached Rene Haas, CEO of British chip designer Arm, in its search for a potential successor to Jensen Huang. Huang resigned after his affair with an alleged Chinese spy. Meanwhile some employees are clamouring for Huang's return – as his fellow tech leader Elon Musk. A sign of Huang's lingering star power, in an industry where so often the fate of each giant company depends on one man. Story by Peter O'Brien.</summary></entry><entry><title>France's school principals say threats and violence have become unbearable</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4398cf4ae6617a993e5b3dd49dfb34b4a72abc032a3e135ca1b278323f093c9</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:13:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:17:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-s-school-principals-say-threats-and-violence-have-become-unbearable--2f046ff96317.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-school-principals-say-threats-and-violence-have-become-unbearable" /><summary type="html">Headteachers gathered across France this Friday, to demonstrate their frustration after nearly two months of student protests that have blockaded high schools. Many of the teachers support the students, but say they feel exhausted and isolated as the violence has surged. They are calling the government to protect them. Story by Vedika Bahl.</summary></entry><entry><title>France protests for fifth Saturday against living costs and heavy-handed policing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a8a0c3e0ac0c47619801bacb6ab50fcdd4ce714fcd9c8f5acade76e2167cea5</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:14:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:15:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-protests-for-fifth-saturday-against-living-costs-and-heavy-handed-policing--dabdfccbee08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-protests-for-fifth-saturday-against-living-costs-and-heavy-handed-policing" /><summary type="html">Different causes are set to come together for one march in Paris this Saturday. Campaign groups, students and Yellow Vest protesters are due to join forces in the capital, bringing together demands on wages, education and civil liberties. But after weeks of demonstrations, union leaders warn that protest fatigue is setting in, while police officers are seeking better compensation for the risk of policing the protests. Story by Jack Pownall.</summary></entry><entry><title>US nationwide flight ground stop: "Our routers got overloaded with data"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6e340fe108e419b2f1a6dbe6fcb3e3bfc9a4712de011d6f7ee5eabb03a36828</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:14:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:14:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-nationwide-flight-ground-stop-our-routers-got-overloaded-with-data--86cafb111fce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-nationwide-flight-ground-stop-our-routers-got-overloaded-with-data" /><summary type="html">On Friday, the Federal Aviation Administration issued a rare nationwide ground stop. More than 8,200 flights, or over 31% of those scheduled in the United States, were canceled. The ground stop lasted nearly five hours and was the longest in the country since September 11, 2001. Officials blamed outdated air traffic communications equipment, and said that there was no evidence of a cyber attack. The airspace is now reopened and flights have resumed.</summary></entry><entry><title>Live: France deploys 70,000 police for new wave of anti-government protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a56ef79eb67d874944b721091ba6044f84b7e367ecd33763dcd438ebd852346a</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:14:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T07:09:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261114-live-france-mobilises-in-fifth-wave-of-student-protests--a833e80bca5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261114-live-france-mobilises-in-fifth-wave-of-student-protests" /><summary type="html">Between 50 and 60 marches are expected in France on Saturday, according to Interior Minister Laurent Nuñez, who plans to mobilise approximately 70,000 police officers and gendarmes across the country. In Paris, the march will commence at 2pm from Place de la République heading towards Place de la Nation via Bastille.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Microsoft says all services 'fully recovered' after global outage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a546eada68c081708c3cc34440f5c8e82cfa9856c8dbab5f5afcbaab1b605be9</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:12:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T06:07:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/technology/20261114-microsoft-says-consumer-products-fully-recovered-business-services-improving--42e4ac49238f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20261114-microsoft-says-consumer-products-fully-recovered-business-services-improving" /><summary type="html">The tech giant confirmed on Saturday morning that all services have recovered ⁠across ‌Teams, Outlook, Copilot and ⁠other applications, ​ending a ‌global outage ‌that ​crippled online communications across businesses and ​governments ​for ​over 24 hours. The US homeland security chief confirmed there was 'no Microsoft link' to the US air traffic stoppage.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>China to host first-ever trilateral meeting between Trump, Xi and Putin next week</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d13e4b4f853aaa964fd88276296b776743075617366c337405a7548109b1e0a8</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:14:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T05:09:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261114-china-to-host-first-ever-trilateral-meeting-between-trump-xi-and-putin-next-week-us-says--a3483041e474.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261114-china-to-host-first-ever-trilateral-meeting-between-trump-xi-and-putin-next-week-us-says" /><summary type="html">The three leaders are scheduled to meet on the sidelines of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation summit in Shenzhen on Thursday, the White House confirmed. US officials said discussions will include nuclear weapons and the war in Iran, but that the war in Ukraine is unlikely to be on the agenda. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky warned the talks could prove a Yalta-like "redistribution of spheres of influence".</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>FAA lifts nationwide ground stop on all US flights</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:429f4713a55b6a9f2a79c6e435a3b573f417f6a6c748a4e0a16e2336516942ad</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:12:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T02:50:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261114-faa-lifts-nationwide-ground-stop-on-all-us-flights--8fca9e8bb835.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261114-faa-lifts-nationwide-ground-stop-on-all-us-flights" /><summary type="html">The United States on Friday lifted an hours-long ground stop at the nation's airports, with top officials explaining that the disruption was not due to a cyberattack or a sweeping Microsoft outage.</summary></entry><entry><title>US flights resume after nationwide ground stop lifted</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5492df9acb0d9e66d8c1dfcd020f31d6c4f86a8f36df546fcc7cca74043424bf</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:12:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T02:35:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261114-us-flights-resume-after-nationwide-ground-stop-lifted-aviation--ee4c7a228fe5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261114-us-flights-resume-after-nationwide-ground-stop-lifted-aviation" /><summary type="html">The United States on Friday lifted an hours-long ground stop at the nation's airports, with top officials explaining that the disruption was not due to a cyberattack or a sweeping Microsoft outage. Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said that US airspace was now "opened up," and blamed "old hardware" for the travel chaos.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Passengers face further cancellations as US flights slowly resume after ground stop</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:253e1f2032eb169b7f1f7b29f6fb2df09aaa3af2e309b438ef6ac944db4634ac</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:12:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T22:43:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-us-air-travel-resumption-will-take-time-after-hours-long-stop--a75173ff3015.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-us-air-travel-resumption-will-take-time-after-hours-long-stop" /><summary type="html">While flights in the United States started resuming on Saturday following the longest nationwide ground stop in 25 years, more than 2,000 flights have been cancelled as airlines work to return to normal operations. Nearly 6,000 flights were cancelled on Friday, with the incident marking only the second time an alert to ground all flights had been issued in US airspace since the 9/11 attacks.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>France secures thrilling Nations Championship victory over South Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b77275012064546722282264b6be483455aaf55397c85615906d9a521129334a</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:14:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T22:39:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20261113-france-hold-on-for-thrilling-nations-championship-win-over-south-africa--23e546b71434.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261113-france-hold-on-for-thrilling-nations-championship-win-over-south-africa" /><summary type="html">France smashed world ⁠champion South ​Africa's hopes of lifting the first Nations Championship trophy on Friday, in a ​21-19 defeat for Les Bleus.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Gambia's Adama Barrow seeks third term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c55cdd0724e3448b75f47ad6cd18c536b251a668d03a09dd16dbfa0daba18b0</id><updated>2026-11-14T15:12:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T21:46:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/gambia-s-adama-barrow-seeks-third-term--167d5d5b0803.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/gambia-s-adama-barrow-seeks-third-term" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme, Gambia's electoral commission has announced the five official candidates for the country's upcoming presidential election. President Adama Barrow is seeking a third term. Tensions continue to rise in Ethiopia following the federal government's appointment of a new head of the Western Tigray region. And the Dakar Youth Olympic Games come to a close after two weeks of intense competition.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry></feed>
